Subject: Remove the switches that are always on

What this does
  Drops the `QJS_REGVM_FAST_COLD`, `QJS_SETNAME_FAST`, `QJS_CTOR_PROTO_FAST`
  and `QJS_DRC_CLOSCYC` switches and their off branches, keeping the default
  path: the seven dedicated handlers are always used, `set_name` always swaps
  an inferred closure name in place, `js_create_from_ctor_cap` always reads an
  instantiated constructor's `prototype` slot directly, and the closure
  self-cycle is always broken at the next reconcile.

Why we need it
  Nothing sets any of the four, and their off branches are dead source that
  would only bit-rot. Every one of them defaults to the same setting the whole
  way through the series.

What it adds
  `REGVM_FAST_HANDLER(name)` is now `regvm_t_##name` unconditionally. No
  behaviour change.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

